1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,570
Good evening, excellence.

2
00:00:01,570 --> 00:00:02,950
Last episode’s riddle?

3
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:04,550
The answer: RACI.

4
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:06,300
Four letters that say who

5
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,050
does what… and who decides.

6
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:09,075
A shipment to a

7
00:00:09,075 --> 00:00:10,100
key customer was late.

8
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:12,150
Procurement said: we ordered it.

9
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:14,320
The warehouse said: nobody told me.

10
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:15,770
Finance said: the request never

11
00:00:15,770 --> 00:00:16,930
reached me to approve.

12
00:00:16,930 --> 00:00:18,525
Everyone did their part… and

13
00:00:18,525 --> 00:00:20,120
the shipment was still late.

14
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:21,180
Who is to blame?

15
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:22,780
The problem isn’t the people…

16
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:24,380
it’s the gap between them.

17
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:26,170
Like a football team with no positions:

18
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:27,548
everyone chases the ball, and

19
00:00:27,548 --> 00:00:28,650
the goal is empty.

20
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:30,460
RACI fills that gap.

21
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:32,460
Responsible: the one who does the work.

22
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,040
Accountable: only one person,

23
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:35,620
with the final say.

24
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:37,230
Consulted before the decision,

25
00:00:37,230 --> 00:00:38,590
Informed after it.

26
00:00:38,590 --> 00:00:39,945
The rule: every task

27
00:00:39,945 --> 00:00:41,300
has one accountable person…

28
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:42,910
not two, and not a committee.

29
00:00:42,910 --> 00:00:44,720
Next to it, the authority matrix:

30
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,530
who approves up to how much.

31
00:00:46,530 --> 00:00:48,540
Department head up to fifty thousand,

32
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:50,370
above that, the general manager.

33
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:53,140
So nobody waits… and nobody oversteps.

34
00:00:53,140 --> 00:00:54,020
Try it tomorrow:

35
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:56,190
pick one process that keeps getting stuck.

36
00:00:56,190 --> 00:00:57,430
Steps in a column,

37
00:00:57,430 --> 00:00:58,670
people in a row,

38
00:00:58,670 --> 00:01:00,270
and put a letter in each cell.

39
00:01:00,270 --> 00:01:01,545
If a step has no

40
00:01:01,545 --> 00:01:02,820
accountable person, or has two…

41
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:04,350
you’ve found the cause of the delay.

42
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:07,100
ISO 9001, clause 5.3,

43
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:09,350
requires roles, responsibilities and authorities

44
00:01:09,350 --> 00:01:11,150
to be assigned, communicated,

45
00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:12,210
and understood.

46
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:13,925
Writing it down isn’t enough…

47
00:01:13,925 --> 00:01:15,640
everyone must know their role.

48
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:17,360
Once you know who’s accountable… how do

49
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:19,080
you know the company is on track?

50
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:20,570
Some companies drive watching

51
00:01:20,570 --> 00:01:22,060
only the money gauge.

52
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:23,730
And there’s a four-sided card

53
00:01:23,730 --> 00:01:25,400
that shows the whole picture.

54
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,120
Know it?

55
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:27,320
Tell me in the comments.

56
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:28,450
Save this episode, and

57
00:01:28,450 --> 00:01:29,580
see you next time

58
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:31,410
on Masaa Al-Tamayoz.
